WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:04.170
-As the trial of his ex-campaign
chairman gets under way

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.704
and his former lawyer
turns on him,

00:00:05.704 --> 00:00:07.640
President Trump
is getting even more desperate

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.108
for the adoration of his crowds.

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:11.411
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:15.781
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.781 --> 00:00:17.984
You can tell the walls
are closing in on Trump

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:20.686
because he keeps reacting
to the Russia investigation

00:00:20.686 --> 00:00:22.389
in increasingly desperate ways.

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:23.789
He's gone all the way
from insisting

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:26.158
he had nothing to do with Russia
to saying there was no collusion

00:00:26.158 --> 00:00:27.994
to claiming that
even if there was collusion,

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.628
it's not a crime,
to demanding that

00:00:29.628 --> 00:00:31.097
the investigation be shut down.

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.831
He's like a murder suspect
who says,

00:00:32.831 --> 00:00:34.000
"I didn't kill anyone,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.169
and besides,
it was self-defense."

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:38.237
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:40.206
And yet the occasional
Republican efforts

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.909
to hold Trump accountable have
not inspired much confidence.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:46.346
For example, you might know
this famous Internet meme,

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:48.381
known as the "This is fine" dog.

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:49.782
It's been around for years.

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:51.417
Well, yesterday,
during a hearing

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:53.085
on Russian
election interference,

00:00:53.085 --> 00:00:54.454
Republican Senator Richard Burr

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:55.955
seemed to have
learned about that meme

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.156
for the very first time.

00:00:57.156 --> 00:01:00.360
-Some feel that we,
as society,

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.529
are sitting in a burning room,
calmly drinking a cup of coffee,

00:01:03.529 --> 00:01:05.665
telling ourselves,
"This is fine."

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.066
That's not fine.

00:01:07.066 --> 00:01:09.169
-Oh, my God.
There is nothing worse

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:12.772
than an old Senator entering
a meme into the public record.

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.407
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:17.143
"Mr. Chairman, I would like
to yield the balance of my time

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.279
to our first witness,
Salt Bae.

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:21.981
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:23.516
Seriously, the President's
trying to shut down

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:24.818
an investigation
into his campaign

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:26.251
for colluding
with a foreign adversary,

00:01:26.251 --> 00:01:27.353
and that's your response?

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.487
Let me put it to you this way --

00:01:28.487 --> 00:01:30.557
some feel
that the Republican Party

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:32.291
is like a frog sipping tea,

00:01:32.291 --> 00:01:33.993
saying,
"The President is a criminal,

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:35.295
but that's none of my business."

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:37.096
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:38.297
And despite --

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:42.134
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:42.134 --> 00:01:45.204
Despite Trump's insistence
that collusion is not a crime,

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:47.940
conspiracy to commit fraud
or violate election laws

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:49.442
very much are crimes.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.410
And many former prosecutors,
even cautious ones,

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:53.413
are beginning to argue that
there's already enough evidence

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:55.948
in the public record
to prove those crimes.

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:58.851
-Are you seeing enough pieces
come to light

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:01.487
in just what is public facing
in this investigation

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:04.456
that you believe there
will be enough to charge someone

00:02:04.456 --> 00:02:06.759
with a conspiracy to coordinate

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:09.095
or receive assistance
from a hostile foreign power?

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:11.297
-Yes, I am.
There are bits and pieces

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:13.599
in the public record
that suggest

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:16.402
that it wasn't just Russians.

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.070
So there's
some unanswered questions,

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.605
but I think
the pieces are there.

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:21.039
-Of course they're there.

00:02:21.039 --> 00:02:23.409
The guy publicly asked Russia
to hack his opponent,

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:24.710
his son
took a meeting with them,

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:26.845
and his closest aides
all look like gangsters

00:02:26.845 --> 00:02:28.081
from a Tex Avery cartoon.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.449
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:31.650
Which is why Trump is getting
increasingly hysterical

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.419
in his calls to end
the investigation

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:35.220
before its findings
become public.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:37.790
Yesterday, he tweeted his
Attorney General Jeff Sessions

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:40.259
"should stop this rigged
witch hunt right now."

00:02:40.259 --> 00:02:41.493
And his lawyer, Rudy Giuliani,

00:02:41.493 --> 00:02:43.262
challenged
Special Counsel Robert Mueller

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:45.431
to come forward
with everything he knows.

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.466
-We believe
that the investigation

00:02:47.466 --> 00:02:48.534
should be brought to a close.

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.102
We think
they're at the end of it.

00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:54.140
They should render their report,
put up -- I mean, I guess,

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.575
if we were playing poker --
we're not -- put up or shut up.

00:02:56.575 --> 00:02:59.511
-It is very lucky you're
not playing poker, Rudy,

00:02:59.511 --> 00:03:02.782
because Robert Mueller
has resting poker face.

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.083
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.784
And you have the face of someone

00:03:05.784 --> 00:03:08.187
who has just
been stuck with a hot poker.

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:10.823
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:13.226
Giuliani then complained
that his team has had to respond

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:16.129
to several accusations,
including accusations leveled

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:19.298
by Trump's former lawyer and
personal fixer Michael Cohen,

00:03:19.298 --> 00:03:22.101
who said last week
that Trump knew in advance

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.437
about that infamous 2016 meeting

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:26.439
at Trump Tower
with Russian officials.

00:03:26.439 --> 00:03:29.342
-We have every reason to believe
they don't have anything,

00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.943
the President
didn't do anything wrong,

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:32.478
they don't have any evidence
he did anything wrong.

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:35.914
They have lots of stuff

00:03:35.914 --> 00:03:37.750
that goes up this alley
and that alley.

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.918
Last week, we were chasing
all these things about Cohen.

00:03:39.918 --> 00:03:41.620
-Yeah, they have lots of stuff.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.623
It's called evidence.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:46.125
If your boat has one leak,
maybe you hit a rock.

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:49.195
If it has 100 leaks,
maybe you have a [bleep] boat.

00:03:49.195 --> 00:03:50.496
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.698
Now, if Trump was directing
his Attorney General,

00:03:52.698 --> 00:03:54.733
who is supposed to be
recused from the investigation,

00:03:54.733 --> 00:03:56.202
to shut down the investigation,

00:03:56.202 --> 00:03:59.172
that seems like a pretty obvious
case of obstruction of justice,

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:02.541
which is why Giuliani tried
to insist it wasn't an order,

00:04:02.541 --> 00:04:04.177
it was just an opinion.

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:07.981
-No, it isn't.
It isn't at all.

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:10.349
It's what it is, as we said
immediately, it's an opinion.

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:11.984
And he used his --

00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:15.521
He used a medium that he uses
for opinions -- Twitter.

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:17.589
And one of the good things
about using that is,

00:04:17.589 --> 00:04:20.326
he's established a clear
sort of practice now

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:23.095
that he expresses
his opinions on Twitter.

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:25.764
He used the word "should."
He didn't use the word "must."

00:04:25.764 --> 00:04:27.567
-I'm sorry.
Do you really think Donald Trump

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.535
is gonna agonize
over the difference

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.604
between "should" and "must"?

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:34.207
A couple weeks ago,
he called his wife Melanie.

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:35.774
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.774 --> 00:04:38.344
Yesterday, he misspelled
the word "smoking."

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:39.745
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.745 --> 00:04:42.882
He's not sitting over parchment,
dipping a quill into an inkwell,

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:44.650
debating which word to use.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:47.253
"Thou art -- no!
Thou shalt."

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:48.821
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.923
Trump just dumps
the ink on the paper

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:53.125
and then smears it around
with his finger.

00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:56.162
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:57.195
Giuliani...

00:04:57.195 --> 00:04:59.632
[ Applause continues ]

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:02.001
Giuliani also insisted
that Trump can't be guilty

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:04.102
of obstruction of justice
because he has the power

00:05:04.102 --> 00:05:06.072
to shut down the investigation
if he wants to.

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:07.640
So where does Giuliani
get that idea?

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.474
He was asked that question
yesterday.

00:05:09.474 --> 00:05:10.876
And if I were his client,

00:05:10.876 --> 00:05:13.379
his answer would not inspire
much confidence.

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:18.450 line:0%
-Of course it's a crime.

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:21.220
No, under Article II
of the Constitution,

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.655
I'm not gonna tell you
my opinion on it

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:23.956
because I haven't really

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.991
gotten to the conclusion
of researching it.

00:05:25.991 --> 00:05:29.195
-You haven't gotten to it?

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:30.763
It's Article II.

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.498
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:35.067
Did you read Article I
and then just take a nap?

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:36.502
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:39.238
It says a lot about your case
when this is the best lawyer

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:40.439
you can get to represent you.

00:05:40.439 --> 00:05:42.742
You want a guy
who sounds like Atticus Finch.

00:05:42.742 --> 00:05:44.810
Rudy sounds like he just
wandered out of Central Park

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:46.512
wearing an open hospital gown.

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:47.680
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.315
I mean, look at him --
he's literally

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:52.184
wiping sweat from his brow.

00:05:52.184 --> 00:05:54.954
Could you imagine
this guy in court?

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:56.989
"The defense may now call
its first witness."

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:58.190
"We're supposed
to have witnesses?

00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.625
Oh, boy!

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.227
Oh, Rudy!

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:04.096
Oh, you done it again, Rudy.
You done it again!"

00:06:04.096 --> 00:06:10.636
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:12.471
"Mr. Giuliani, are you ready
for a press conference?"

00:06:12.471 --> 00:06:14.340
"Yeah, just bring me
my sweat rag!

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:18.277
[ Laughter ]

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:19.645
Apparently, all of this

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:21.881
has taken an emotional toll
on Trump.

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:23.983
CNN reports that
people inside the White House

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:25.617
say he's been in a dark place.

00:06:25.617 --> 00:06:27.453
So, welcome aboard.

00:06:27.453 --> 00:06:29.688
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.688 --> 00:06:30.890
Yeah, I mean...

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.958
In response,
he's been seeking solace

00:06:32.958 --> 00:06:34.760
and emotional support
from his crowds,

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:37.230
which is why he held another one
of his public therapist sessions

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:39.164
on Tuesday in Florida,
where he once again

00:06:39.164 --> 00:06:42.134
relived the glory days
of his campaign.

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:43.435
-They said it couldn't be done.

00:06:43.435 --> 00:06:45.137
It was actually done
quite easily.

00:06:45.137 --> 00:06:47.105
We won quite handily.

00:06:47.105 --> 00:06:49.708
We were never off center stage.

00:06:49.708 --> 00:06:51.644
You know what that means, right?
The debates.

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:54.480
We never left center stage.

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:56.249
We won every farm state.

00:06:56.249 --> 00:06:58.150
You got to see
that middle of that --

00:06:58.150 --> 00:06:59.618
Wasn't even the middle.

00:06:59.618 --> 00:07:03.255
It was about everything but
the little corners of each side.

00:07:03.255 --> 00:07:05.658
But you have to see,
that is all red.

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:08.794
Republican red.
Beautiful Republican red.

00:07:08.794 --> 00:07:11.029
And you know what they were
asking on election day?

00:07:11.029 --> 00:07:13.165
"Where did all these people
come from?"

00:07:13.165 --> 00:07:15.033
You know where they came from?

00:07:15.033 --> 00:07:16.535
They came from the heart.

00:07:16.535 --> 00:07:22.074
They came from people that
were never happy with anybody

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:23.843
until we came along.

00:07:23.843 --> 00:07:27.379
-"They were never happy with
anybody until we came along."

00:07:27.379 --> 00:07:29.515
Trump talks about himself
the way a romance novel

00:07:29.515 --> 00:07:31.550
talks about
the sexy pirate character.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:32.819
[ Laughter ]

00:07:32.819 --> 00:07:34.386
"She was never happy
with anybody...

00:07:34.386 --> 00:07:36.222
until he came along.

00:07:36.222 --> 00:07:37.356
He made her so lustful,

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:39.091
she had to wipe the sweat
from her brow."

00:07:39.091 --> 00:07:40.359
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:41.861
This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:45.231
[ Cheers and applause ]

